WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.050
- Everybody, it is time to
crack open our show vault

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:05.610
and share something we've
never shown before today.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.640
Earlier this year, Hollywood power couple,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.390
Nick Offerman and Megan Mullally

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:12.270
dialed in from separate
rooms of the same house.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.672
That's a real true thing.

00:00:13.672 --> 00:00:15.421
Megan and I got to talking

00:00:15.421 --> 00:00:17.850
about how we got started in music

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.000
and she shared some
pretty revealing things

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.220
so check it out.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.350
I feel like all people,

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.670
like, no matter what part
of the industry you're in,

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.190
we all started like musical theater,

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.650
like when we were kids
and doing stuff like-

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:29.483
Did you do that?

00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:31.230
Did you start like musical
theater when you're young?

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:35.750
- [Megan] I did, I used to
sing, my parents would go out

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.990
and I'd put on Barbara Streisand
and Judy Garland records.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:39.823
- [Host] Yes.
- [Megan] 'Cause apparently

00:00:39.823 --> 00:00:43.154
my parents were a gay male couple, ch.

00:00:43.154 --> 00:00:45.124
(laughs)
(slaps thighs)

00:00:45.124 --> 00:00:49.030
And I would just like sing
one song over and over again

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:52.260
until I could sing it
exactly like the record.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.260
And then first time I sang
in public, I was a senior

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:00.810
in high school and I went to
this apisca paleon school,

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.510
private school, we had chapel every day,

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:07.270
which is so bizarre and embarrassing.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:12.270
And so I was encouraged
by the people who like,

00:01:13.377 --> 00:01:17.840
did such things to get up in
front of the entire high school

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.770
and belt out three show
tunes, which I did.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.720
And I was incredibly nervous
and it ended up going well,

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.130
but I had choreographed a song
from the musical, Chicago,

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.300
called, Razzle Dazzle.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.240
- [Host] Yeah.
- [Megan] And during it,

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.740
I went over and sat on
the principal's lap,

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.880
which was like a huge, crazy
thing to do at the time.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.480
And then Nick and I were just
in Oklahoma City recently,

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.880
and we actually found the
cassette tape of me singing

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:44.720
that.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.133
- [Host] What?
- Which is-

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:47.480
- [Megan] Yeah, it was crazy.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.313
- That is so cool.
- [Megan] Yeah.

00:01:48.313 --> 00:01:51.010
- I randomly, I think
it was my mom that said,

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.550
oh my God, I randomly found
a VHS of like me doing

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:54.710
something like in high school.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.280
And I was like, what?

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.113
That's what-

00:01:57.113 --> 00:01:59.070
And I'm the same as you, I used
to memorize stuff like that.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.155
Like I would sing Don't Rain On My Parade.

00:02:01.155 --> 00:02:02.910
Like I sang it so much.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:04.530
I wanted to sing it again.
- That the first song

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.593
I sang, wait, that's the first
- [Host] Oh.

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:08.080
song I sang in chapel.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.450
- That's my favorite.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.032
Literally when I was at
Radio City Music Hall

00:02:11.032 --> 00:02:11.865
(coughs)
and we were on tour

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.490
and I cover songs all
the time, I was like,

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.140
I will cover this song
(claps)

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:15.973
in this place
(claps)

00:02:15.973 --> 00:02:17.340
and it will be magical.
(claps)

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.034
I love her so much.
- [Megan] Oh my god.

00:02:19.034 --> 00:02:22.070
- [Host] No, that's a great.
- [Megan] That's (indistinct)

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:24.490
The first I sang was
Don't Rain On My Parade.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:25.572
Then I sang People.

00:02:25.572 --> 00:02:26.405
- [Host] Okay.

00:02:26.405 --> 00:02:27.810
- [Megan] And then Razzle
Dazzle from Chicago,

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.030
but they're all not razzle-dazzle as much,

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.580
but Don't Rain On My Parade, and People

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:33.510
are really hard songs to sing, you know,

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.540
for your first time
- [Host] Yes.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:35.829
It's like Weird and Grieve.
- [Megan] singing in public.

00:02:35.829 --> 00:02:36.662
- [Host] And Don't Rain On My Parade.

00:02:36.662 --> 00:02:39.450
I also secretly love that
you kind of gave your, either

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.241
teacher or principal, a lap dance and

00:02:41.241 --> 00:02:43.961
(laughs)
it was kind of amazing.

00:02:43.961 --> 00:02:45.320
- [Megan] (indistinct) really dazed,

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:46.862
I mean the word lap dance
(laughs)

00:02:46.862 --> 00:02:48.543
(claps)
hadn't been invented.

00:02:49.409 --> 00:02:52.738
- See, he invented rap and
you invented lap dances.

00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:53.571
You are the perfect couple.

00:02:53.571 --> 00:02:54.404
[Crowd] Woo.

